<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://leiqianstat.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://leiqianstat.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-09-09T21:46:31+00:00</updated><id>https://leiqianstat.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Lei Qian</title><entry><title type="html">Hello</title><link href="https://leiqianstat.github.io/blog/2026/hello/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Hello"/><published>2026-09-09T16:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-09T16:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://leiqianstat.github.io/blog/2026/hello</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://leiqianstat.github.io/blog/2026/hello/"><![CDATA[<p>This is a first post written with the al-folio <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">post</code> layout.</p> <p>New entries go in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">_posts/</code> as <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">YYYY-MM-DD-title.md</code>. After that, they show up on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a> page and in the latest-posts list on the home page.</p> <p>Markdown, math, and code all work. For example, an inline expression such as \(E = mc^2\) renders with MathJax when <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">enable_math</code> is on.</p> <p>Replace this file when you publish a real note.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="blog"/><category term="notes"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Opening this blog for research notes and writing]]></summary></entry></feed>